		<wp:meta_value><![CDATA[About 1 hour]]></wp:meta_value>
		</wp:postmeta>
							<wp:postmeta>
		<wp:meta_key><![CDATA[_recipe_storage]]></wp:meta_key>
		<wp:meta_value><![CDATA[Keep in an airtight container.]]></wp:meta_value>
		</wp:postmeta>
							<wp:postmeta>
		<wp:meta_key><![CDATA[_recipe_bakers_note]]></wp:meta_key>
		<wp:meta_value><![CDATA[Cookie can get very hot after baking. Let the cookies cool before tasting.]]></wp:meta_value>
		</wp:postmeta>
							<wp:postmeta>
		<wp:meta_key><![CDATA[_recipe_ingredients]]></wp:meta_key>
		<wp:meta_value><![CDATA[1½ cups all-purpose flour
1½ teaspoons salt
½ teaspoon baking soda
½ teaspoon baking powder
½ cup brown sugar
½ cup granulated white sugar
½ cup vegetable shortening
1⁄3 cup water
2 tablespoons vanilla extract
Flaky salt, for topping (optional)]]></wp:meta_value>
		</wp:postmeta>
							<wp:postmeta>
		<wp:meta_key><![CDATA[_recipe_method]]></wp:meta_key>
		<wp:meta_value><![CDATA[Whisk the flour, baking soda, baking powder, and salt together in a bowl.
In another bowl, beat the shortening and sugars until it becomes sandy.
Mix in the dry ingredients just until combined.
Beat in the water and vanilla extract.
Cover and chill the dough for 30 minutes. Meanwhile, heat the oven to 350°F (175°C).
Scoop the dough onto a lined baking sheet, leaving space between cookies.
Bake for 10–12 minutes, until the edges are golden and the centers still look soft.
Sprinkle with flaky salt, if desired. Cool on the tray for 5 minutes, then move to a rack.]]></wp:meta_value>
		</wp:postmeta>
